{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices during the initial 10-15 day horizon following a price drop, failing to capture the depth of the crash (e.g., forecasting ~76-77 while true prices fall to ~67-70).",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion lag: The model exhibits a 'sticky' upward drift that ignores immediate downward momentum; forecasts must be adjusted downward by 5-8 EUR for the first two weeks when history shows a sustained decline.",
    "Anticipate delayed V-shaped recovery: The model underestimates the magnitude and speed of the rebound in the final 10 days (forecasting ~77 vs true ~80); apply a positive correction of 2-3 EUR to the tail end of the forecast horizon.",
    "Decouple sentiment from short-term trend: High sentiment scores (1.00) in the history do not prevent immediate price drops; do not rely on positive sentiment to justify upward forecast adjustments during active downtrends.",
    "Reduce forecast volatility: The model's linear progression is too smooth compared to the actual high-volatility swings; introduce a wider confidence interval or a non-linear decay factor to better match the jagged true outcome path."
  ]
}
